IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `da-property`
IMPORT `da-vehicles`

-- Duties Act 2008 (WA) -- the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as parameters (the Q&A layer).
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The baseline (da-property.l4, da-vehicles.l4) was written from one seat, the buyer, who meets three different
-- duties the Act puts on three different people: the transferee or purchaser of land (transfer duty and foreign transfer
-- duty, Schedule 1, s 205K), the person to whom a vehicle licence is granted or transferred (vehicle licence duty,
-- s 232(1)), and the acquirer of an interest in a landholder (landholder duty, Chapter 3). Those three are the roles. The
-- seller of land owes no transfer duty under the provisions encoded (Schedule 1 column 4 names the transferee or
-- purchaser), the dealer's liability (s 252) is not encoded, and the Commissioner is never a seat: what the Commissioner
-- may or must do appears only as what it means for the buyer.
--
-- SITUATIONS (graffiti design D8). Within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that situation's fact
-- straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when it does not hold, without reading anything else.
-- The questions of one situation share ONE input, the same name, type and @desc, so the form asks it once. All are for the
-- buyer of land:
--   - `I am buying a lot off the plan` (Chapter 6A): is it a concessional off-the-plan agreement, how much concession,
--     and the time to apply for it (s 266O).
--   - `a foreign person is among the buyers` (Chapter 3A Part 2): the foreign transfer duty, and the time to lodge the
--     foreign transfer duty declaration (s 205M).
--   - `every buyer is a concessional first home owner` (s 142A): the time to seek the first home owner rate by
--     reassessment (s 144(2)). "Is my purchase a first home owner concessional transaction" does not take it: it answers
--     no for a buyer who is not a first home owner, which is the answer that buyer wants, and it reads the baseline's own
--     field for it.
-- A question that arises in every situation of its role takes no situation input.
--
-- The rules are the baseline's. This module calls the baseline's functions and restates none. Every answer type carries
-- `does not arise for you`. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Duties Act 2008 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am buying a home or other land in Western Australia`
    `I am buying a vehicle, or having its licence granted or transferred to me`
    `I am acquiring shares in a company that may hold land in Western Australia`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Months` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    months HAS `number of months` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Time to pay answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `pay` HAS `the time to pay` IS A `Time to pay`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

§§ `For the buyer of land, and the acquirer of shares`

§§§ `s 15, Schedule 2 Division 1 -- what is dutiable, and the general rate`

@export Is what I am buying dutiable property for transfer duty (Duties Act 2008 (WA) s 15)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the property` IS A `Kind of property` @desc What you are buying: land in Western Australia, land outside it, a right, a chattel in Western Australia, a Western Australian business asset, or shares in a company
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is what I am buying dutiable property for transfer duty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a home or other land in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Is what I am buying dutiable property` `the property`)
    WHEN `I am acquiring shares in a company that may hold land in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Is what I am buying dutiable property` `the property`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The general rate is also the rate of landholder duty (s 184(1)), so the acquirer of shares may ask it too.
@export What duty would I pay at the general rate on this dutiable value (Duties Act 2008 (WA) s 26, Schedule 2 Division 1)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER @desc The dutiable value, in dollars: for land, the greater of the price and the unencumbered value (s 27); for landholder duty, your share of the company's Western Australian land and chattels (s 188)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What duty would I pay at the general rate on this value` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a home or other land in Western Australia` THEN amount (`What duty would I pay at the general rate` `the dutiable value`)
    WHEN `I am acquiring shares in a company that may hold land in Western Australia` THEN amount (`What duty would I pay at the general rate` `the dutiable value`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the buyer of a home or other land`

§§§ `ss 20, 27, 142 -- who pays, the dutiable value, and the first home owner rate`

@export As the buyer, am I the person liable to pay the transfer duty (Duties Act 2008 (WA) s 20, Schedule 1)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am the transferee or purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the property is transferred, or agreed to be transferred, to you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I the person liable to pay the transfer duty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a home or other land in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Must I pay the transfer duty` `I am the transferee or purchaser`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the dutiable value of my purchase: the greater of the price and the unencumbered value (Duties Act 2008 (WA) s 27)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc Your purchase: the price and the unencumbered value, the kind of land and region, whether it is residential, whether each buyer is a concessional first home owner, who the buyers are, and, for a lot bought off the plan, the stage, the scheme, the day the agreement was made (as YYYYMMDD), and the Chapter 6A facts
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the dutiable value of my purchase` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a home or other land in Western Australia` THEN amount (`What is my dutiable value` `the purchase`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my purchase a first home owner concessional transaction (Duties Act 2008 (WA) s 142(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc Your purchase: the price and the unencumbered value, the kind of land and region, whether it is residential, whether each buyer is a concessional first home owner, who the buyers are, and, for a lot bought off the plan, the stage, the scheme, the day the agreement was made (as YYYYMMDD), and the Chapter 6A facts
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my purchase a first home owner concessional transaction under s 142` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a home or other land in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Is my purchase a first home owner concessional transaction` `the purchase`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What transfer duty must I pay on my purchase, after any first home owner rate and off-the-plan concession (Duties Act 2008 (WA) ss 26, 142, 143, 266K, Schedule 2)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc Your purchase: the price and the unencumbered value, the kind of land and region, whether it is residential, whether each buyer is a concessional first home owner, who the buyers are, and, for a lot bought off the plan, the stage, the scheme, the day the agreement was made (as YYYYMMDD), and the Chapter 6A facts
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What transfer duty must I pay on my purchase` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a home or other land in Western Australia` THEN amount (`What transfer duty must I pay` `the purchase`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- Situation: each buyer is a concessional first home owner (s 142A), so the first home owner rate can be sought.
@export Up to how many months after completion may I apply for the first home owner rate by reassessment (Duties Act 2008 (WA) s 144(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `every buyer is a concessional first home owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and each person buying with you, is a concessional first home owner under the First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (s 142A)
      `I applied for the grant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied for a first home owner grant
      `months from completion to the grant being paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months after completion the grant was paid
GIVETH A `Months`
`Up to how many months after completion may I seek the first home owner rate by reassessment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a home or other land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `every buyer is a concessional first home owner`
        THEN months (`Up to how many months after completion may I seek the first home owner rate` `I applied for the grant` `months from completion to the grant being paid`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Chapter 3A Part 2 -- foreign transfer duty`

@export Am I a foreign individual for foreign transfer duty (Duties Act 2008 (WA) s 205A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the buyer` IS A Buyer @desc You: whether you are an Australian citizen, hold a permanent visa, or hold a special category visa
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I a foreign individual for foreign transfer duty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a home or other land in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Am I a foreign individual` `the buyer`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- Situation: a foreign person is among the buyers (s 205K(1)(b)).
@export What foreign transfer duty must I (and my co-buyers) pay on my purchase (Duties Act 2008 (WA) Chapter 3A Part 2, ss 205K, 205L, 205O, 266K)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a foreign person is among the buyers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, or anyone buying with you, is a foreign individual: not an Australian citizen, and holding neither a permanent visa nor a special category visa (s 205A)
      `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc Your purchase: the price and the unencumbered value, the kind of land and region, whether it is residential, whether each buyer is a concessional first home owner, who the buyers are, and, for a lot bought off the plan, the stage, the scheme, the day the agreement was made (as YYYYMMDD), and the Chapter 6A facts
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What foreign transfer duty must we pay on the purchase` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a home or other land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `a foreign person is among the buyers`
        THEN amount (`What foreign transfer duty must I pay` `the purchase`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how many months must I lodge a foreign transfer duty declaration (Duties Act 2008 (WA) s 205M)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a foreign person is among the buyers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, or anyone buying with you, is a foreign individual: not an Australian citizen, and holding neither a permanent visa nor a special category visa (s 205A)
GIVETH A `Months`
`Within how many months must I lodge the foreign transfer duty declaration` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a home or other land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `a foreign person is among the buyers`
        THEN months `Within how many months must I lodge a foreign transfer duty declaration`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Chapter 6A -- the off-the-plan concession`

-- Situation: I am buying a lot off the plan, in a scheme still to be registered (ss 266F(1)(a), 266FA(1)(a)).
@export Is my agreement a concessional off-the-plan agreement (Duties Act 2008 (WA) Chapter 6A, ss 266F, 266FA)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am buying a lot off the plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying, from the owner of land to be subdivided by a strata or community titles scheme, a lot in the scheme on which there will be a new dwelling (Chapter 6A)
      `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc Your purchase: the price and the unencumbered value, the kind of land and region, whether it is residential, whether each buyer is a concessional first home owner, who the buyers are, and, for a lot bought off the plan, the stage, the scheme, the day the agreement was made (as YYYYMMDD), and the Chapter 6A facts
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my agreement a concessional off-the-plan agreement under Chapter 6A` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a home or other land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `I am buying a lot off the plan`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my agreement a concessional off-the-plan agreement` `the purchase`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much off-the-plan concession do I get (Duties Act 2008 (WA) s 266L)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am buying a lot off the plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying, from the owner of land to be subdivided by a strata or community titles scheme, a lot in the scheme on which there will be a new dwelling (Chapter 6A)
      `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc Your purchase: the price and the unencumbered value, the kind of land and region, whether it is residential, whether each buyer is a concessional first home owner, who the buyers are, and, for a lot bought off the plan, the stage, the scheme, the day the agreement was made (as YYYYMMDD), and the Chapter 6A facts
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much off-the-plan concession do I get under s 266L` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a home or other land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `I am buying a lot off the plan`
        THEN amount (`How much off-the-plan concession do I get` `the purchase`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how many months of completion must I apply for the off-the-plan concession (Duties Act 2008 (WA) s 266O)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am buying a lot off the plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying, from the owner of land to be subdivided by a strata or community titles scheme, a lot in the scheme on which there will be a new dwelling (Chapter 6A)
GIVETH A `Months`
`Within how many months of completion must I apply for the off-the-plan concession` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a home or other land in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `I am buying a lot off the plan`
        THEN months `Within how many months must I apply for the off-the-plan concession`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 23, 25 -- lodging and paying`

@export Within how many months after liability arises must I lodge the transfer document or a transfer duty statement (Duties Act 2008 (WA) s 23)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Months`
`Within how many months must I lodge the transfer document or statement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a home or other land in Western Australia` THEN months `Within how many months must I lodge`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for not lodging the transfer document, statement or foreign transfer duty declaration in time (Duties Act 2008 (WA) ss 23, 205M)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for not lodging in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a home or other land in Western Australia` THEN amount `What is the most I can be fined for not lodging`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export By when must I pay the transfer duty (Duties Act 2008 (WA) s 25)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `it is a conditional agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract is a conditional agreement
      `it must be registered under the Transfer of Land Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a document for your purchase must be registered under the Transfer of Land Act 1893
      `it is a subdivision or issue of title conditional agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract is conditional on a subdivision or on the issue of a title
GIVETH A `Time to pay answer`
`By when must I pay the transfer duty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a home or other land in Western Australia` THEN `pay` (`By when must I pay the duty` `it is a conditional agreement` `it must be registered under the Transfer of Land Act` `it is a subdivision or issue of title conditional agreement`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the buyer of a vehicle`

§§§ `Chapter 5, ss 229, 230, 232, 236 -- vehicle licence duty`

@export Must I pay vehicle licence duty on the vehicle I am buying (Duties Act 2008 (WA) ss 229, 230, 232)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `it must be licensed under the Vehicles Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle must be licensed under the Road Traffic (Vehicles) Act 2012
      `it is a caravan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a caravan
      `the licence is granted or transferred to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the licence is being granted in your name or transferred to you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I pay vehicle licence duty on this vehicle` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a vehicle, or having its licence granted or transferred to me` THEN `yes if` (`Must I pay vehicle licence duty` `it must be licensed under the Vehicles Act` `it is a caravan` `the licence is granted or transferred to me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What vehicle licence duty must I pay on the vehicle I am buying (Duties Act 2008 (WA) s 236)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the vehicle's dutiable value` IS A NUMBER @desc For a used vehicle, what it might reasonably sell for in the open market, in dollars (s 238)
      `is a heavy vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a heavy vehicle
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What vehicle licence duty must I pay on this vehicle` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying a vehicle, or having its licence granted or transferred to me` THEN amount (`What vehicle licence duty must I pay` `the vehicle's dutiable value` `is a heavy vehicle`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the acquirer of shares in a company`

§§§ `Chapter 3 -- landholder duty`

@export Must I pay landholder duty on the shares I am acquiring (Duties Act 2008 (WA) Chapter 3, ss 155(2), 161, 163)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the company` IS A Company @desc The company whose shares you are acquiring: whether it is listed, the value of its land assets in Western Australia (with linked entities'), and the value of its Western Australian land assets and chattels
      `interest before` IS A NUMBER @desc Your interest (with associates) before the acquisition, as a percentage
      `interest after` IS A NUMBER @desc Your interest (with associates) after the acquisition, as a percentage
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I pay landholder duty on these shares` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am acquiring shares in a company that may hold land in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Must I pay landholder duty` `the company` `interest before` `interest after`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What landholder duty must I pay on the shares I am acquiring (Duties Act 2008 (WA) ss 184, 186, 188)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the company` IS A Company @desc The company whose shares you are acquiring: whether it is listed, the value of its land assets in Western Australia (with linked entities'), and the value of its Western Australian land assets and chattels
      `interest before` IS A NUMBER @desc Your interest (with associates) before the acquisition, as a percentage
      `interest after` IS A NUMBER @desc Your interest (with associates) after the acquisition, as a percentage
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What landholder duty must I pay on these shares` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am acquiring shares in a company that may hold land in Western Australia` THEN amount (`What landholder duty must I pay` `the company` `interest before` `interest after`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
